  "result": "The gate passed with **OK** on run 3 of 6: 22 witnesses, 18 names, and the composition with `NRS_484B_257_1_o1` evaluated.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **UNUSED_CLAIM:** I ran it on the untouched skeleton by mistake, so this run was wasted.\n2. **VACUOUS:** all witnesses passed, but some leaves in the obligation's restated selection were never exercised:\n   - the police and signal exception leaves;\n   - \"a sign governs X\".\n3. **OK**, after two fixes:\n   - **Rule:** the through-highway test now excludes X itself (`¬ same c3 X`). X never has an observed `st_lane_enters`, so a sign governing X left that test unknown.\n   - **Witnesses:** I added branch_15 to branch_18 so the obligation's copy of those leaves decides a verdict.\n\n**How the rule reads the node**\n- **Applicability:** there is an intersection X and a carrier c where:\n  - the subject is in X and moving, and has stayed in X since it entered from c;\n  - at that entry:\n    - c enters X;\n    - a stop or yield sign governs c or X;\n    - no police officer and no working traffic signal governs c or X;\n    - `NRS_484B_257_1_o1` was complied with.\n- **Obligation:** it repeats that whole selection for every (X, c) pair. For every other vehicle v on a through highway, the subject must not touch v. It must also not keep moving while a closest approach within `p.conflict_horizon` falls below `p.conflict_centre_clearance`. v counts if either:\n  - it entered X from that highway, or\n  - it is approaching on one of that highway's lanes as an immediate hazard.\n- **Entry observation:** I pin it with `rises` plus a nested `since`, which matches the record's \"occupied c at the observation before\".\n- **No narrowings declared.**\n\n**Weak points**\n- **branch_18 uses unusual data:** the only way to exercise the obligation's copy of the traffic-membership and police-role leaves was a scene with two overlapping carriers. One of them is recorded on two highways.\n- **I didn't read `o1`:** the instructions put its file off limits. The witnesses pass, but which instant `o1` judges is inferred from those results, not checked against its formula.\n\nFiles are in `library/` under the repo root:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_257_1_o2.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_257_1_o2.lean`\n- `task_result.md`, in the working directory",
